When , ANY authenticated user may reach the dashboard — but ONLY in the
Development environment (never Testing or Production). A local-dev convenience;
defaults to  so it never loosens a deployed environment.

A cache-aside decorator over the raw (ADR 0007). It wraps the inner and, for every method, tries the free in-memory first (System.Text.Json round-trip of the Application read model), calls the inner client on a miss, then stores the successful result under a stable cinora:tmdb:* key with a per-resource TTL. Handlers depend only on and are oblivious to caching (SRP: the raw client does HTTP + mapping; this decorator adds cache-aside + graceful degradation). Three invariants from ADR 0007:
never cache a null/empty miss (a 404 details response and an empty search page are re-fetched so a later populate is picked up);
degrade, never error — any cache get/set failure is logged and the request falls through to the inner client, so a cache outage never surfaces as an error;
±10% per-write TTL jitter so co-created hot keys do not expire in unison (stampede guard).
Internal: the composition root registers it wrapping the concrete .
